    "text": "Cape Town's winter storm season runs May–August. North-westerly frontal systems bring strong winds and heavy rain, particularly affecting coastal roads, the Cape Peninsula, and low-lying flood plains. Berg wind events in autumn bring extreme fire risk to the northern suburbs and winelands."
